<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi{{{Case.First_Name__c}}},&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Thank you for contacting Qantas Customer Care regarding your experience in {DEPARTURE} on {{{Case.Email_Departure_Date_Time__c}}}.<br />
<br />
I’m sorry to hear that we were unable to carry you on flight QF{{{Case.Flight_Number__c}}}. I understand how frustrating this must have been for you and would like to apologise for any impact this had on your plans.<br />
<br />
<strong>Things don’t always go to plan</strong><br />
<br />
When flights have been overbooked, airlines are responsible to provide customers with alternative flights to get them to their destination or offer a full refund if they decide they no longer wish to travel.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If requesting compensation add:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
While we can’t provide compensation on this occasion, if you had any unexpected expenses because of the &lt;delay/cancellation&gt;, your travel insurance policy may cover these sorts of situations.<br />
<br />
Please let us know if you’d like us to provide you with an insurance letter to assist with any claim.<br />
<br />
<strong>We value your opinion</strong><br />
<br />
Customer feedback plays an important role in our continuous improvement process so that we can provide you with exceptional service from start to finish.<br />
<br />
I wanted to assure you that your comments about the way this was handled have been forwarded to our Airport Management for review.</body>
